  "body": "## What is in it\n\nThis PR adds research notes in `docs/research/heidenhain/`. The notes tell which words, cycles and cycle parameters each HEIDENHAIN TNC control accepts, and from which NC software version.\n\n- `README.md`: the method, the coverage and the top findings.\n- `dialects.md`: a proposal for `controller.identity` values, capability flags and profiles (control + NC software → flags).\n- `differences.md`: the common language, the additions of each series, post-relevant features with \"introduced / changed / removed\", and the Q-parameter lists of cycles 200, 203, 205, 207 and 209.\n- `differences-by-version.md`: the new-function entries of each NC software version (generated, short pointers only).\n- `cycles.md`: 211 cycle numbers with the HEIDENHAIN name, a purpose, the DIN/ISO code, the option, the versions and a reference.\n- `inventory.md`: each manual with its ID, title, edition date and download URL.\n- `picomax-55-review.md`: the review of the two HEIDENHAIN posts and `fehlmann-picomax55.mch` against the Fehlmann manual and the machine parameters.\n\n## Method\n\n- The sources are the public HEIDENHAIN user manuals and the \"Overview of New and Modified Software Functions\" documents from the TNCguide portal.\n- The text of each PDF was extracted with `pdftotext -layout`, and scripts searched the text.\n- Each fact has a HEIDENHAIN document ID and a PDF page. A gap is marked \"unsure\" or \"not found\".\n- The Q lists (B3) come from the example block that starts with the cycle's own number and name, up to the next NC block. Each row has the manual ID and the PDF page.\n- Section C applies the \"not TNC 410\" marks of the shared ISO manual 345 940-22. A bullet that names a different software version than its heading is removed.\n- Each profile in `dialects.md` has a source column. A cell without full evidence is \"unknown\".\n\n## What is not in it\n\n- No manual, no extracted manual text and no local path. The files hold facts with document references and short phrases only.\n- No access codes, passwords or file names that identify the single machine. The review keeps the MP numbers and values.\n- No code change.\n\n## How it feeds the issues\n\n- #4095: `dialects.md` is the proposal for the dialect selection.\n- #4093 and #4094: the version thresholds for `FUNCTION DWELL` and for Q395/Q208 are in `differences.md` (B2, B3).\n- #4085, #4086, #4087 and #4088: the review gives the evidence (MP values and manual pages).\n- #3095: the review lists what to test on the real iTNC 530 340490-03.\n\n## Review fix (head 5a1fddf15)\n\n- B3 made again; the old rows that mixed in other cycles are gone.\n- TNC 320 Q208/Q395 at 77185x-01 (was -05) in all copies.\n- TNC 410 section of `differences-by-version.md` removed; TNC 410 rows in `cycles.md` and the TNC 410 profile corrected.\n- TNC 426/430 profile split at 280 474 (cycle 205) and 280 476 (M140, cycle 247).\n- Picomax review link in `dialects.md` fixed.\n\nGate: none. The PR changes only Markdown files under `docs/research/`, and no `cargo xtask gate` step covers that folder.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nRefs #4095\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
